== Notes ==
* There is only one Crawl Space room per floor. Thus, if Isaac finds two trapdoors with ladders on the same floor, they will lead to the same Crawl Space. When Isaac exits the Crawl Space, he will come out from the entrance he came in from. {{dlc+|r}} Creating a Crawl Space within a Crawl Space with {{p|XXI - The World?}} will just take Isaac back to the original one.{{dlc-}}
* Entering a Crawl Space in the {{R|Boss Rush}} room and exiting it after the time limit has expired will transport Isaac back to the {{E|Mom}} Boss room.
* There is no map in the Crawl Space, similar to the {{R|Black Market}}, the {{R|I AM ERROR}} room, the {{R|Devil Room}}, and the {{R|Angel Room}}.
** This is because the Crawl Space does not technically occupy a fixed location on the floor relative to other rooms; Isaac is, in a sense, teleported to the Crawl Space when he touches the trapdoor. Possibly related to this, should Isaac enter a crawl space from a Devil Room, upon exiting he will emerge back in the regular map.
* Be careful when using {{I|The Poop}}, as in certain situations, The Poop can block the exit and trap Isaac.
* Crawl spaces can appear in [[Greed mode]] as well.
* {{dlc|nr}}It is possible to enter {{R|Black Market}}s through a Crawl Space even when there is no path to it. By using two bombs, Isaac can clip out of bounds and then walk underneath the Crawl Space room.
** {{dlc+|r}} Leaving a Crawl Space from any side where no exit exists brings Isaac to {{R|I AM ERROR}} instead. It is now significantly more difficult to clip out of bounds, and can't be done with just two bombs.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|a}} With {{i|Continuum}}, if Isaac shoots downward in a Crawl Space, his tears will continuously accelerate and may loop many times (over 20), regardless of his range.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|a}} Rocks with Crawl Spaces under them will flash while holding the {{t|Shiny Rock}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|a}} The trinket {{t|Stud Finder}} adds an additional 1 in 200 chance for a Crawl Space to appear when a rock is destroyed.
** With {{i|Mom's Box}} or a {{A|Golden Trinket}} it becomes 1 in 100.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} The Crawl Space that appears by using a {{p|Chaos Card}} on {{E|Great Gideon}} always has the same design even if another Crawl Space was encountered.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} One Crawl Space layout contains two items, one of which is entirely enclosed by walls. The following are ways to obtain the seemingly off-limits item:
** Teleport to it with {{I|Stitches}};
** Grab it with {{I|Mr. ME!}};
** Jump through the wall with {{I|How to Jump}};
** Using {{i|Void}} with {{i|Birthright}} when playing as {{c|Apollyon}} has a 10% chance to create a copy of the item after being absorbed by Void;
** Absorb it with {{I|Moving Box}}, then place it in another room;
** Clipping through the wall with {{I|Pluto}};
** Cloning the item using {{I|Diplopia}} and grabbing the copy created underneath.
*** This applies as well for {{i|Crooked Penny}}.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} Crawl Spaces can be found during the {{E|Mother's Shadow}} sequence. She will follow Isaac into them, so care must still be taken to avoid her charge.{{dlc-}}
** The sequence may contain key blocks, usually with a key nearby. If a key is in your inventory when entering the crawl space, it will get transferred to your key pool, rendering a nearby key block impossible to remove.
* {{dlc+|r}} Crawl spaces can still be found on floors during the [[Ascent]] to {{s|Home}}.{{dlc-}}

