== Trivia ==
* The layout of the Crawl Space is a direct visual reference to the treasure rooms in the Legend of Zelda for the NES.
* Crawl Spaces are referred to within the game files as "Item Dungeons".

== Bugs ==
{{bug|If Isaac's hitbox is small enough (by using [[One Makes You Smaller]] pills), it's possible to travel through the walls and ceiling to access the {{R|Black Market}}. In Afterbirth+, the walls are much harder to clip through, but it can still be done with high speed and help of the stairs or flight.}}
{{bug|dlc=r|If Isaac uses a {{p|XXI - The World?}} card inside a {{R|Black Market}} and enters it, he will be taken to the crawl space that leads to the Black Market. If he then tries to leave the crawl space from here, he will be spawned back inside it making exiting to the main floor no longer possible. If this is done on the {{s|Chest}}, {{s|Dark Room}}, {{s|The Void}}, or {{s|Home}} floors it will result in a soft lock since Isaac cannot leave through the trap door that usually spawns in the {{R|Black Market}}.}}
{{bug|If Isaac teleports to an {{r|I AM ERROR}}, {{r|Devil Room}}, or {{r|Angel Room}} from a Crawl Space, and then enters a Crawl Space from that room, Isaac will be unable to exit the crawl space. He will be permanently stuck unless he can teleport out.}}

